Use a non-HW placeholder pix_fmt in the H.264 buffer source filter.

neatvnc 0.9.6 creates the libavfilter "buffer" source with pix_fmt=drm_prime
and a NULL hw_frames_ctx, expecting to set the real hw_frames_ctx later via
av_buffersrc_parameters_set(). This worked through FFmpeg 7. FFmpeg 8 enforces
the hw_frames_ctx requirement at avfilter_graph_create_filter() itself, so
the encoder now fails with:

    Setting BufferSourceContext.pix_fmt to a HW format requires
    hw_frames_ctx to be non-NULL!

Switching the placeholder to a non-HW format (yuv420p) lets the create call
pass; av_buffersrc_parameters_set() then overrides format -> drm_prime *and*
attaches hw_frames_ctx in one step before avfilter_graph_config() validates.

Reported upstream behaviour, kept local until neatvnc tags a fix.

--- a/src/enc/h264/ffmpeg-impl.c
+++ b/src/enc/h264/ffmpeg-impl.c
@@ -204,12 +204,15 @@ static int h264_encoder__init_buffersrc(struct h264_encoder_ffmpeg* self)
 {
 	int rc;

-	/* Placeholder values are used to pacify input checking and the real
-	 * values are set below.
+	/* Placeholder values are used to pacify input checking; the real
+	 * width/height/format/hw_frames_ctx are set below via
+	 * av_buffersrc_parameters_set(). FFmpeg 8 rejects pix_fmt=drm_prime
+	 * (a HW format) without an attached hw_frames_ctx at create time,
+	 * so a non-HW placeholder is used here.
 	 */
 	rc = avfilter_graph_create_filter(&self->filter_in,
 			avfilter_get_by_name("buffer"), "in",
-			"width=1:height=1:pix_fmt=drm_prime:time_base=1/1", NULL,
+			"width=1:height=1:pix_fmt=yuv420p:time_base=1/1", NULL,
 			self->filter_graph);
 	if (rc != 0)
 		return -1;
